SUMMARY:Economic Theory – David Frankel (MBS) – Predicting Participatio
 n
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3062
DESCRIPTION:David Frankel: “Predicting Participation”\nDavid Frankel | 
 Melbourne Business School Faculty\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/
 BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nWe study participation games\, in which a 
 set of players decide whether or not to take part in an activity that is w
 orthwhile only if enough others participate. We show that any equilibrium 
 selection criterion that is continuous\, nontrivial\, label-invariant\, an
 d has a mild independence property must predict tthat an agent will play a
  best response to some fixed\, common\, symmetric “fictional beliefs” 
 over the number of others who participate.
END:VEVENT
